set.body:
Purpose: freeze the target architecture before implementation changes continue.

Decisions to record in docs/plans/multivar-operator-core.md and the public module contract:
- One directed operator type Op[From, To, Role, Evidence]. Role states meaning; Evidence is a static capability tag backed by a runtime certificate bound to value identity.
- Algebraic dual and metric adjoint are distinct named operations.
- FunctionalFrame W: K -> C* is the universal latent parameter; scores XW and axes QW are derived.
- OperatorProgram is the universal mathematical program, with a closed BaseObjective ADT, typed variables, parameterizations, penalties, constraints, and a result contract.
- Operator policies remain upstream of the variational program; ModelSpec owns fitted preprocessing, estimation, selection, and fold-safe lifecycle.
- Compatibility adapters may delegate to the new core during migration but may not remain an independent numerical engine.

Required inventory:
- map every production consumer of MvMetric, MvMap, DualityDiagram, GenPca, PairedGmd, MultisetObjectives, CPCA, kernel/Nystrom, multiblock, row geometry, plans, and fit artifacts;
- assign every consumer to a finite migration child;
- specify evidence preservation/downgrade rules and result-equivalence vocabulary;
- define unsupported surfaces explicitly.

Acceptance:
- architecture decision is committed and cross-linked from module-relations;
- inventory has no unowned production consumer;
- negative type examples cover nominal-space and primal/dual mismatches;
- no implementation deletion begins until this issue and the core primitive issue are closed.
